  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Aosta.\u00a0</p>\r\n<p>After the fall of the western empire, Aosta was retaken by Pepin the Short and, under Charlemagne, became an important point on the <em>Via Francigena\u00a0</em>on its course from Aachen to Italy.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Augusta Praetoria (modern Aosta) was a settlement of the Salassi conquered by Rome in 25 B.C. From 24 B.C. a colony of 3,000 Roman military veterans occupied the city of Augusta Praetoria Salassorum and it became the capital of the province Alpes Graies from 11 B.C.",
